      "productId": "openmrs",
      "question": "When a user adds a sticky note in the patient chart, what code runs from the frontend request down to the database write? List the frontend function that sends the request, the server-side REST handler, the core service implementation, and the data-access method.",
      "generation": "g-b59a21",
      "kind": "partial",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "A sticky note is stored as a standalone `Obs` (an observation) on the configured `stickyNoteConceptUuid` concept. Here is the full path from the React button to the Hibernate write.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**1. Frontend request**\n- The note is composed in `StickyNoteModal`, whose Save button calls `handleSave`; for a new note it awaits `createStickyNote(patientUuid, trimmed, stickyNoteConceptUuid)` [1].\n- `createStickyNote` is the function that sends the request: it uses `openmrsFetch` to `POST ${restBaseUrl}/obs` with a JSON body of `person`, `concept`, `value` and `obsDatetime` [2]. (`updateStickyNote` and `deleteStickyNote` hit `/obs/{uuid}` [3].)",
          "citations": [
            1,
            2,
            3
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**2. Server-side REST handler**\n- The `/ws/rest/v1/obs` resource is `ObsResource1_8`, annotated `@Resource(name = RestConstants.VERSION_1 + \"/obs\", ...)` [4]. The POST is dispatched to its `save(Obs)` override, which creates the delegate via `newDelegate()` (a bare `new Obs()`) [5] and delegates to the core service with the change message `\"REST web service\"` [6]. It then re-reads the saved obs by id so the response reflects the persisted row.",
          "citations": [
            4,
            5,
            6
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**3. Core service implementation**\n- `ObsServiceImpl.saveObs(Obs, String)` validates the obs, requires the `ADD_OBS` privilege for a new obs (`ensureRequirePrivilege`) [7], and since a new sticky note has no `obsId`, takes the `saveNewOrVoidedObs` branch [8].\n- `saveNewOrVoidedObs` handles any complex-obs concept data, calls the DAO, then saves obs groups [9]. (The editing path instead goes through `saveExistingObs`, which writes a new row, voids the old one, and sets the previous-version link [10].)",
          "citations": [
            7,
            8,
            9,
            10
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**4. Data-access method**\n- The DAO method is `HibernateObsDAO.saveObs(Obs)`: it recursively saves unsaved group members, then persists the obs with `HibernateUtil.saveOrUpdate(sessionFactory.getCurrentSession(), obs)` [11]. This is the call that issues the insert/update against the `obs` table via the Hibernate session. The DAO contract is declared as `ObsDAO.saveObs(Obs)` [12].",
          "citations": [
            11,
            12
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "```archify\n{\n  \"schema_version\": 2,\n  \"diagram_type\": \"sequence\",\n  \"meta\": { \"title\": \"Sticky note save: frontend to database\" },\n  \"participants\": [\n    { \"id\": \"ui\", \"type\": \"frontend\", \"label\": \"StickyNoteModal\" },\n    { \"id\": \"resource\", \"type\": \"frontend\", \"label\": \"sticky-note.resource\" },\n    { \"id\": \"rest\", \"type\": \"backend\", \"label\": \"ObsResource1_8\" },\n    { \"id\": \"service\", \"type\": \"backend\", \"label\": \"ObsServiceImpl\" },\n    { \"id\": \"dao\", \"type\": \"backend\", \"label\": \"HibernateObsDAO\" },\n    { \"id\": \"db\", \"type\": \"database\", \"label\": \"obs table\" }\n  ],\n  \"messages\": [\n    { \"from\": \"ui\", \"to\": \"resource\", \"y\": 70, \"label\": \"createStickyNote\" },\n    { \"from\": \"resource\", \"to\": \"rest\", \"y\": 140, \"label\": \"POST /obs\" },\n    { \"from\": \"rest\", \"to\": \"service\", \"y\": 210, \"label\": \"saveObs(obs, message)\" },\n    { \"from\": \"service\", \"to\": \"dao\", \"y\": 280, \"label\": \"saveObs(obs)\" },\n    { \"from\": \"dao\", \"to\": \"db\", \"y\": 350, \"label\": \"saveOrUpdate\" },\n    { \"from\": \"service\", \"to\": \"rest\", \"y\": 420, \"label\": \"saved Obs\", \"variant\": \"return\" },\n    { \"from\": \"rest\", \"to\": \"resource\", \"y\": 490, \"label\": \"obs JSON\", \"variant\": \"return\" },\n    { \"from\": \"resource\", \"to\": \"ui\", \"y\": 560, \"label\": \"snackbar and mutate\", \"variant\": \"return\" }\n  ]\n}\n```",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "text": "A note on the concept-typing detail: because the frontend sends `value` as a plain string and `person`/`concept` only (no `encounter`), the obs is a standalone, non-encounter obs — which matches the `isStandaloneStickyNote` filter used when reading notes back packages/esm-patient-notes-app/src/sticky-notes/sticky-note.resource.ts.",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
